fest (names, normalized keys, content sha256, groups, roles)\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"role\": \"final_mteb_data\",\n    \"path\": \"resources/final/mteb_final.npz\",\n    \"sha256\": \"dc3c957fdbcd4f242e653789c7538e1fe0260821da48de14749a52e610ec94c7\",\n    \"source\": \"MTEB results repo @6dabbcc68c28ea5f180ce7df79347b3ca9cc6383 (CC0-1.0), preprocessed (latest-revision-dir main_score per model/task, normalized, hashed, family-grouped, plane- and history/held-out-split by hash order) ; float64 values/observed/role arrays\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"role\": \"final_mteb_manifest\",\n    \"path\": \"resources/final/mteb_final_manifest.json\",\n    \"sha256\": \"da916cc4d9b6dbc06a51e3ac08fb7ec011d94492847619cb7939dc7ef449cd23\",\n    \"source\": \"MTEB results repo @6dabbcc68c28ea5f180ce7df79347b3ca9cc6383 (CC0-1.0), preprocessed (latest-revision-dir main_score per model/task, normalized, hashed, family-grouped, plane- and history/held-out-split by hash order) ; evaluator-private provenance manifest (names, normalized keys, content sha256, groups, roles)\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"role\": \"final_oll_data\",\n    \"path\": \"resources/final/oll_final.npz\",\n    \"sha256\": \"bc800d1571d363fc466b6c3be36f9b5562c95f744431704fa7c9c0436d7a7b78\",\n    \"source\": \"open-llm-leaderboard/contents @9c09a7cae43334062a82cb164f2ef255013dafa2 data/train-00000-of-00001.parquet (sha256 f13a7061e63133bc8745d89f8c7a56148584940ede22d3b27e21cad1e078dca5), raw scores of 6 benchmarks, deduplicated, family-group split ; float64 values/observed/role arrays\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"role\": \"final_oll_manifest\",\n    \"path\": \"resources/final/oll_final_manifest.json\",\n    \"sha256\": \"8284be64e37d61a1fa3a241376e419cdd9025db5e6f5eeb6b720af76740a23b1\",\n    \"source\": \"open-llm-leaderboard/contents @9c09a7cae43334062a82cb164f2ef255013dafa2 data/train-00000-of-00001.parquet (sha256 f13a7061e63133bc8745d89f8c7a56148584940ede22d3b27e21cad1e078dca5), raw scores of 6 benchmarks, deduplicated, family-group split ; evaluator-private provenance manifest (names, normalized keys, content sha256, groups, roles)\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"role\": \"dependency_pins\",\n    36 task/capture.py\n  1036 task/evaluate.py\n  1054 task/evaluate_final.py\n   108 task/task.md\n  2234 total\nresults/ideas:\n01_greedy_conditional_variance_benchmark_selection_with_low_rank_imputation\n02_wrapper_cv_error_benchmark_selection_with_robust_quantile_transformed_stacked_imputation\n03_robust_monotone_link_latent_skill_predictor_with_a_optimal_selection_added_to_the_incumbent_stack\n\nresults/ideas/01_greedy_conditional_variance_benchmark_selection_with_low_rank_imputation:\nactive_idea.json\nactive_rubrics.json\nagent_claude_20261111_114015.log\ncapture.py\nevaluate.py\nidea_bundle.json\nidea_generation_wrapper_output.log\nmemory.md\nprogram_0\nprogram_1\nprompt.md\nrubric_status.json\ntarget_rubrics.json\ntask.md\nwrapper_output.log\n\nresults/ideas/02_wrapper_cv_error_benchmark_selection_with_robust_quantile_transformed_stacked_imputation:\nactive_idea.json\nactive_rubrics.json\nagent_claude_20261111_114722.log\ncapture.py\nevaluate.py\nidea_bundle.json\nidea_generation_wrapper_output.log\nmemory.md\nprogram_0\nprogram_1\nprompt.md\nrubric_status.json\ntarget_rubrics.json\ntask.md\nwrapper_output.log\n\nresults/ideas/03_robust_monotone_link_latent_skill_predictor_with_a_optimal_selection_added_to_the_incumbent_stack:\nactive_idea.json\nactive_rubrics.json\nagent_claude_20261111_120053.log\ncapture.py\nevaluate.py\nidea_bundle.json\nidea_generation_wrapper_output.log\nmemory.md\nprogram_0\nprogram_1\nprompt.md\nrubric_status.json\ntarget_rubrics.json\ntask.md\nwrapper_output.log\n\ntask/program_0:\nprogram_spec.toml\nsrc\n\ntask/program_0/src:\nprogram.py\n\ntask/resources:\nfinal\nsearch\n# Reference Query Plan\n\n## Central topic\nChoosing a small subset of k benchmarks to run on a new model and imputing its scores on the remaining benchmarks from a historical model-by-benchmark score matrix (MTEB, HELM Lite, Open LLM Leaderboard), evaluated by held-out-model normalized RMSE against random selection, ridge and permuted-control baselines.\n\n## Core methods\n- greedy conditional-variance (Gaussian/low-rank) benchmark subset selection\n- EM-estimated Gaussian covariance with conditional-mean imputation of missing scores\n- wrapper cross-validated forward selection of benchmarks\n- rank-Gauss (quantile) transform with range clipping\n- per-target NNLS stacked ensemble of imputers\n- monotone-link latent-skill model with Huber MAP and Laplace posterior\n- A-optimal experimental-design selection\n\n## Comparators\n- random benchmark selection\n- greedy ridge regression on selected benchmarks\n- permuted-control baseline\n- low-rank matrix completion / probabilistic matrix factorization\n- item-response-theory style latent ability models for LLM evaluation\n- benchmark-sparsification work (metabench, tinyBenchmarks)\n- observational scaling laws and Sloth skill scaling laws\n\n## Benchmarks\n- MTEB (embedding models x tasks)\n- HELM Lite (core scenarios)\n- Open LLM Leaderboard (IFEval, BBH, MATH Lvl 5, GPQA, MUSR, MMLU-PRO)\n\n## Method shifts visible in the run\n- from pure conditional-variance Gaussian imputation (nRMSE 1.067 in search) to quantile-transformed wrapper-selected NNLS-stacked imputation (nRMSE 1.028)\n- adding a monotone latent-skill member and A-optimal selector to the stack gave identical search score to the stacked incumbent (no measurable gain)\n- final sealed evaluation nRMSE 0.562 overall, with MTEB error decreasing as k grows (0.787 at k=2 to 0.638 at k=20)\n\n## Result-driven themes\n- few benchmarks recover the rest only modestly: skill over random selection is small (final 0.016) while gain over greedy ridge is larger (0.099)\n- prediction difficulty varies by leaderboard (HELM 0.50, Open LLM 0.48, MTEB 0.70)\n- diminishing returns in k on MTEB\n- permuted-control gap shows that cross-benchmark structure is real\n- low-rank / latent-skill structure in model-by-benchmark matrices\n\n25\n@Article{Valipour2022DyLoRAPT,\n booktitle = {Conference of the European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics},\n title = {DyLoRA: Parameter-Efficient Tuning of Pre-trained Models using Dynamic Search-Free Low-Rank Adaptation},\n@Article{Li2025LLMsCE,\n booktitle = {arXiv.org},\n title = {LLMs Can Easily Learn to Reason from Demonstrations Structure, not content, is what matters!},\n@Article{Kim2025OneRT,\n booktitle = {arXiv.org},\n title = {One ruler to measure them all: Benchmarking multilingual long-context language models},\n@Article{Onal2024GaussianSW,\n booktitle = {arXiv.org},\n title = {Gaussian Stochastic Weight Averaging for Bayesian Low-Rank Adaptation of Large Language Models},\n@Article{Saranathan2025SubLIMESS,\n booktitle = {Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics},\n title = {SubLIME: Subset Selection via Rank Correlation Prediction for Data-Efficient LLM Evaluation},\n@Article{Abdullah2025EvolutionOM,\n booktitle = {arXiv.org},\n title = {Evolution of meta's llama models and parameter-efficient fine-tuning of large language models: a survey},\n@Article{Lutz2020RiskAO,\n booktitle = {Physical Therapy},\n title = {Risk Adjustment of the Modified Low Back Pain Disability Questionnaire and Neck Disability Index to Benchmark Physical Therapist Performance: Analysis From an Outcomes Registry.},\n@Article{Rutunda2026LargeLM,\n booktitle = {Nature Health},\n title = {Large language models for frontline healthcare support in low-resource settings},\n@Article{Maimon2025FromBT,\n booktitle = {Transactions of the Association for Computational Linguistics},\n title = {From Benchmarks to Skills: Low-Rank Factors for LLM Evaluation},\n@Article{Zhao2025MoRAMM,\n booktitle = {arXiv.org},\n title = {MoRA: Missing Modality Low-Rank Adaptation for Visual Recognition},\n@Article{Subramani2025SimBASB,\n booktitle = {Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing},\n title = {SimBA: Simplifying Benchmark Analysis Using Performance Matrices Alone},\n@Article{Wu2025MappingOI,\n booktitle = {International Conference on Learning Representations},\n title = {Mapping Overlaps in Benchmarks through Perplexity in the Wild},\n@Article{Rullo2025InterdisciplinaryDA,\n booktitle = {Journal of Medical Internet Research},\n title = {Interdisciplinary Development and Fine-Tuning of CARDIO, a Large Language Model for Cardiovascular Health Education in HIV Care: Tutorial},\n@Conference{Azeta2024InteractiveML,\n booktitle = {2024 International Conference on Emerging Trends in Networks and Computer Communications (ETNCC)},\n title = {Interactive Machine Learning Framework for Predicting Asthma Health Conditions Using XGBoost},\n@Book{Phan2023EvaluatingAO,\n booktitle = {International Conference on Information and Knowledge Management},\n title = {Evaluating and Optimizing the Effectiveness of Neural Machine Translation in Supporting Code Retrieval Models: A Study on the CAT Benchmark},\n@Article{Han2025LLM4SGAL,\n booktitle = {IEEE Transactions on Machine Learning in Communications and Networking},\n title = {LLM4SG: Adapting Large Language Model for Scatterer Generation via Synesthesia of Machines},\n@Inproceedings{Linzmayer2026AggregateBS,\n booktitle = {medRxiv},\n title = {Aggregate benchmark scores obscure patient safety implications of errors across frontier language models},\n@Article{Chen2025ClassifyingAS,\n booktitle = {Journal of Medical Internet Research},\n title = {Classifying American Society of Anesthesiologists Physical Status With a Low-Rank–Adapted Large Language Model: Development and Validation Study},\n@Inproceedings{Ardabili2025LargeLanguageModelMR,\n booktitle = {medRxiv},\n title = {Large-Language-Model Mortality Risk Stratification in the Intensive Care Unit: A Benchmark Against APACHE II},\n@Article{Jimenez2025AnES,\n booktitle = {Latin American Computing Conference / Conferencia Latinoamericana En Informatica},\n